Z||000003||Wolfhound||05-12-2001||12:29 PM||||Thanks for the complement Buzz, When the page was new it was insane and occupied most of mine and Garys time, but a labor of love. <BR>It has now slowed with growth to be a managable thing.<P>The military will not release list (Privacy Act they clam), But I think it,s laziness which I cannot tolerate.<P>The list has done majical things, It has allowed children to meet and comunicate with people who knew and served with their dads before they were KIA.<BR> Unknown to many in the states is the fact that Canada and Australia served in Vietnam  and well I might add.<P>Your right, It,s the dang trailer!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||05-12-2001||12:41 PM||||Sqoach, It,s an 86SE, 2.8 Paint by Peach automotive or something like that. Really bad, enough over spray to paint another car. I fired it up a bit ago and it has a slight rod rattling at startup that clears. it,s runnig about 50 psi cold. I maybe can save it by changing out the bearings. It,s iffy. Seats are perfect.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||05-13-2001||09:44 PM||||visited your web page today. Very nice. Looks like a lot of work but glad to see people doing it. I've had a little trouble getting info about my unit from D.C. too but I was a Marine over there and Popasmoke was a big help. There is some info on that site about getting unit rosters from the time period you were there. Think you can only send two requests per year. By the way, your guestbook was full. Thanks again for the help with the qtr pnl.<BR>Don & Jane||||reg||14
